1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,300
Fifty thousand, credited. By the twentieth… gone. Where?

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:05,900
Let's follow one salary.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,900
Rent. EMI. Bills. You saw those coming.

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,300
Food, travel, one OTT plan. Life happens.

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,900
A SIP. Future you says thanks.

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,000
And then… eight thousand. Sixteen percent. No name. No category.

7
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:23,000
Never one big thing. Chai. A late-night order. A forgotten renewal.

8
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:30,200
Not a budget problem. A habit problem. By month-end, memory fades. A few seconds a day sticks.

9
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:37,200
TrackMyRupee keeps it tiny. Type it — swiggy 320. It fills in the details. You check, then add.

10
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:43,200
Every rupee gets a name. Forget a day? An optional 9 pm nudge.

11
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:47,400
Try the free demo. Link in bio.
